<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orbelian dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th–15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Orbelians were an Armenian princely family who ruled much of Syunik and Vayots Dzor from the 13th to the 15th century. Branch of a family that had served the Georgian crown, they settled in Syunik under the Zakarid princes and later served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>. Their rule saw a cultural revival, and the historian Stepanos Orbelian wrote a history of Syunik.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/orbelian-dynasty.jpg" alt="Orbelian dynasty" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Princes_Bughta_and_Burtel_Orbelians.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
